WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.277
Quarantine is a useful pattern when values are questionable but not safely correctable.

00:00:05.277 --> 00:00:10.357
The source remains intact. Issue flags identify what needs attention.

00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:14.117
A view or table exposes the review subset.

00:00:14.117 --> 00:00:20.597
After review, records can be corrected, approved, or excluded according to policy.

00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:24.037
This is often safer than automatic replacement.

00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:31.357
A quarantine pattern separates questionable records from trusted analytical output without deleting evidence.

00:00:31.357 --> 00:00:38.532
Views are useful for reusable cleaning logic because they let you expose a consistent cleaned representation

00:00:38.532 --> 00:00:41.387
while keeping raw source data intact.

00:00:41.387 --> 00:00:44.701
That improves reproducibility and auditability.
